{"id": "EUVD-2026-76415", "enisaUuid": "69f8e8d1-0656-3b7e-8f63-ddc1b4c81eff", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/ionic: Embed counter driver data in rdma_counter allocation\n\nCommit 7e53b31acc7f (\"RDMA/core: Create and destroy rdma_counter using\nrdma_zalloc_drv_obj()\") requires drivers implementing counter ops to\nembed struct rdma_counter in a driver-specific struct, register its size\nvia INIT_RDMA_OBJ_SIZE, and provide a counter_init callback.\n\nThe ionic driver was merged without this adaptation, causing a NULL\npointer dereference in alloc_and_bind() since rdma_zalloc_drv_obj()\nallocates zero bytes when size_rdma_counter is unset.\n\nConsolidate struct ionic_counter into a new struct ionic_rdma_counter\nthat embeds struct rdma_counter, replace the xarray with a lightweight\nida for ID allocation, and add the required counter_init and\nINIT_RDMA_OBJ_SIZE declarations.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:43:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:48:00", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c98197ee3cd28288da13dc9881bb9e74daa7cbbc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/08b8630b557828aedb1d9ef0a6e2ec421f334ee2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cf3ebd89e754015625fee90aa938f6bc79a2c974"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89509", "GHSA-p644-p7x2-xc3f"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b200df6-c379-30c0-8fb9-98e90eaa7a17", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "75f6d5e6-ee5b-323e-a7c8-24644db057c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ea4c399642b85dc30f44d90ee805c6a18fa03062 <08b8630b557828aedb1d9ef0a6e2ec421f334ee2"}, {"id": "87a2b7d3-24be-3dbe-ba51-2f019390fd3c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "87f356b7-1a33-3b1a-867a-7b5e6729a6d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "a1b1f3a4-0456-34ba-8be9-9f3197652cc5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "e6da677b-4118-330f-838d-23a095376ae0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "f6733bf1-e295-3f02-ba11-b26586023947", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ea4c399642b85dc30f44d90ee805c6a18fa03062 <c98197ee3cd28288da13dc9881bb9e74daa7cbbc"}, {"id": "f7195b7e-962d-3a3d-af36-a525e3243dda", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ea4c399642b85dc30f44d90ee805c6a18fa03062 <cf3ebd89e754015625fee90aa938f6bc79a2c974"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b2f1df44-5711-3923-a602-645fe037311f", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}